SPU: look SPU_PCSAMPLE up once, not on every MFC channel access (open upstream PR, imported as is).

mfc_for, which every SPU channel read and write goes through, called getenv("SPU_PCSAMPLE") each time while the
variable is unset. getenv takes the C library's environment lock, and in Resistance 3's gameplay the five SPU host
threads queue on it: a 5 s `sample` showed about 430 of their 1600 busy samples in getenv and that lock's wait
(__findenv_locked, _os_unfair_lock_lock_slow <- getenv <- mfc_for).

Scripted run (gameplay, same scene, host frame log, distinct frames): idle 16.4 -> 19.1 fps, turning 17.0 -> 23.3
fps in one A/B pair (runs of this scene spread by a few fps); getenv gone from the SPU threads' stacks.
test_spu_mfc_env_once.c is in the PR.

Upstream: PR #243 (drop this file when the pin contains it).

---

